If anyone would like to take this on for Hacktoberfest, it shouldn't require too many changes.

### Overview

Since we already fetch the public SSH key, but don't display it, it should be a matter of simply changing the SSH command's [`displayer`](https://github.com/digitalocean/doctl/blob/master/commands/displayers/key.go).

### How to fix it

We need to update the key `displayer` to show the public key field. The changes to the displayer would be as follows,

```diff
--- a/commands/displayers/key.go
+++ b/commands/displayers/key.go
@@ -31,13 +31,13 @@ func (ke *Key) JSON(out io.Writer) error {

 func (ke *Key) Cols() []string {
        return []string{
-               "ID", "Name", "FingerPrint",
+               "ID", "Name", "FingerPrint", "PublicKey",
        }
 }

 func (ke *Key) ColMap() map[string]string {
        return map[string]string{
-               "ID": "ID", "Name": "Name", "FingerPrint": "FingerPrint",
+               "ID": "ID", "Name": "Name", "FingerPrint": "FingerPrint", "PublicKey": "Public Key",
        }
 }

@@ -46,7 +46,7 @@ func (ke *Key) KV() []map[string]interface{} {

        for _, k := range ke.Keys {
                o := map[string]interface{}{
-                       "ID": k.ID, "Name": k.Name, "FingerPrint": k.Fingerprint,
+                       "ID": k.ID, "Name": k.Name, "FingerPrint": k.Fingerprint, "PublicKey": k.PublicKey,
                }

                out = append(out, o)
```

We'd also need to check that the tests still pass, and potentially update them. Our tests can be run from the root of the repo with `go test ./...`. We have both regular Go unit tests, and a suite of integration tests.

